      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "「改（以下四行原朱）"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Editorial note set in the gutter: 改, 'revised', followed in reduced type by the 1928 editor's parenthesis （以下四行原朱）, meaning that the following four lines are in red ink in the original. The opening bracket 「 stands above 改 and its closing 」 is printed at the foot of the last of those four columns, under 成 in 金子、親成. The four columns the note governs are the ones immediately to its left: the 大參事 column, the 權大參事 column, the 少參事 column, and the unheaded column that continues the junior councillors — counted on the leaf, exactly four."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "三日市改原朱註"
      }
